    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214-a1">

                <pb facs="0540" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg450"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    1069.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">DUKE DECAZES TO
                        MR. WASHBURNE</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Versailles</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi>,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor herewith to send
                    yon, in compliance with the desire expessed by yon, a statement of the names and
                    addresses of the Lafayette family, together with their degrees of relationship
                    to the general. I thought I could not do better, in order to obtain this
                    information, than to address Mr. O. de Lafayette, a deputy in the National
                    Assembly, and, in transmitting it to me, he has begged me to express the
                    gratitude felt by the Lafayette family in consequence of the adoption of the
                    resolution by the Congress of the United States which you were pleased to bring
                    to my notice.</p>
                <p>Accept the assurances, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>DECAZES.</item>
                            <item>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washburne</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Minister of the United States.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
